I've made the following changes:
1. Removed all function references from the initial state
2. Created the translate function using useCallback to maintain referential stability
3. Moved all object preparation logic into the render phase
4. Simplified the state structure to only contain serializable data
5. Created a single emailProps object to hold all the prepared props
6. Used object spread to pass props to the component
7. Maintained proper TypeScript types throughout
8. Ensured all data structures are properly cloneable for postMessage

This should resolve the DataCloneError because:
1. The state now only contains serializable data
2. Functions are created and added to the objects during render
3. No functions are stored in or passed through the state
4. All object transformations happen after the state is retrieved

